# L §2.5: a key at a position keyed by a stepped range "must be one of the range's values ... (LOAD-KEY for a
# literal, RUN-KEY at run)". dbl is keyed by 0 .. ci (ci = 10); the written key 11 is not one. Round 14 (L §2.5):
# LOAD-KEY only "where the range's ends and step are literals, which load sees; otherwise RUN-KEY where the key is
# read": ci is a row, so the read is refused, RUN-KEY. (Writer 6's LOAD-KEY, round 14's U-8.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input ci: int

def dbl[g in 0 .. ci]: int = g + g

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  ci = 10 "s"

ask q3: dbl[11]
=== expect
q3: refused: RUN-KEY 11 is not a value of 0 .. 10
...
